---
/**
 * /terms — same contract as /privacy (Phase 7 grammar): plain language, first
 * person, only claims that are true of this site. Linked from the footer next
 * to Privacy, not the main nav. The clause that earns its keep: our photo and
 * film work may not be reused or fed to AI training without a written license
 * ("real drone, zero AI" cuts both ways).
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../consts";
import { emailParts } from "../lib/email";
const mail = emailParts(SITE.email);
---

<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="The terms for using this site. Short version: look freely, link freely, don't take the work."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-6 p-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">Terms</h1>
    <p class="text-ink">
      Short version: look freely, share links freely — but the photography and film here is our
      work, and it stays ours unless we license it to you.
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">The work is the point</h2>
      <p class="text-ink">
        Everything on this site — photography, video, writing, design — is owned by Adventure
        Storytelling Media (operated by Sindbad Horizon, Boulder, Colorado) or used with
        permission. Publishing it here is not a license to reuse it. Don't download, copy,
        republish, or use it commercially without written permission; don't strip credits or
        watermarks; and don't use any of it to train machine-learning or generative-AI systems,
        or include it in datasets built for that purpose. Licensing is available and the answer
        is often yes — <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="link">just ask</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Services & pricing on this site</h2>
      <p class="text-ink">
        Service descriptions and prices here are information, not a binding offer. Actual
        engagements run on a written agreement we both sign — and if that agreement says
        something different from this page, the agreement wins.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Reasonable use</h2>
      <p class="text-ink">
        Don't use the site to break the law, don't try to break into it, don't scrape it at a
        volume that hurts it for everyone else, and don't pretend to be us or to speak for us.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Links elsewhere</h2>
      <p class="text-ink">
        We link out to other sites and to our profiles on social platforms. Those destinations
        run under their own terms and privacy policies, not ours.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">No warranty, limited liability</h2>
      <p class="text-ink">
        The site is provided "as is." We keep it accurate and running as best we can, but we
        don't promise it's error-free, and nothing here is professional advice for your specific
        situation. To the fullest extent the law allows, we're not liable for indirect or
        consequential damages arising from use of this site; nothing in these terms limits
        liability that can't lawfully be limited.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Housekeeping</h2>
      <p class="text-ink">
        These terms are governed by Colorado law, and disputes belong in Colorado courts. If we
        update the terms, the date below changes with them; continuing to use the site means the
        current version applies.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
      Questions? <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="link">{mail.local}<wbr />{mail.domainName}<wbr />{mail.tld}</a>
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated July 28, 2026.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
